# ChatGPT's side panel takes the current tab once, when its page loads, and never listens for
# another: Chrome shows each tab its own panel page. Cra has one panel page per window, so after
# a tab switch ChatGPT kept reading the first tab. Such a panel now loads again for the tab Cra
# shows (ChatGPT keeps each tab's conversation, so going back finds it).
budget rss=700 stalls50=5
from://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/SidePanelExtension
relaunch
from://open?url=${PAGE}?n=first
wait 2
from://open?url=${PAGE}?n=second
wait 2
from://debug?extensionAction=${SIDE_PANEL_EXTENSION_ID}
expect-log side panel shows ${SIDE_PANEL_EXTENSION_ID} in Default
wait 2
from://debug?sidePanelJS=chrome.storage.session.set({bindOnly:true}).then(()=>location.reload())
wait 2
from://debug?sidePanelJS=following
expect-log side panel evaluates following to second$
from://action/nextTab
wait 2
from://debug?sidePanelJS=following
expect-log side panel evaluates following to first$
from://action/nextTab
wait 2
from://debug?sidePanelJS=following
expect-log side panel evaluates following to second$
from://debug?removeExtension=${SIDE_PANEL_EXTENSION_ID}
wait 1
reject-log fault:
